  "summary": "I’m an IT professional with a strong foundation in programming, database development, and system analysis, currently pursuing my B.S. in Computer Science at Texas A&M University–Corpus Christi. I hold an AAS in Computer Programming from Del Mar College, along with multiple certificates in IT Essentials, Programming, and Interactive Game Technology.\n\nMy technical experience includes C++, Java, SQL, Visual Studio, VS Code, Unity, Unreal Engine, and hands‑on project work building relational databases and software tools. During my internship at Del Mar College, I designed and tested SQL databases, developed programs to process and print data, and performed quality assurance on database operations — experience that strengthened both my development and problem‑solving skills.\n\nI also bring several years of experience in healthcare and customer‑service environments, where I learned to communicate clearly, document accurately, and work within strict compliance frameworks such as HIPAA. These roles taught me reliability, patience, and how to support people in high‑stakes situations — strengths that translate directly into IT support, troubleshooting, and user‑focused technical roles.\n\nI’m passionate about technology, continuous learning, and building solutions that make systems more efficient and user‑friendly. I’m actively seeking opportunities in IT Support, Junior Software Development, Systems Administration, or related roles where I can contribute, grow, and expand my technical expertise.\n\nIf you’re looking for someone who is motivated, adaptable, and committed to developing as a technology professional, I’d be glad to connect.",
